    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82864" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγ-άζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγή</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spring, gush forth</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγάζει τὸ διαυγὲς ἐν ὄμμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>APl.</u>
					4.310
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Damoch.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγάζοντες μαστοί, φλέβες
				πηγάζουσαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.31
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.324
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.
			cogn., <i>gush forth with</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νᾶμα μέλισσα πηγάζει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.404
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ῥεῖθρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					<u>All.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[Ζεὺς] π. ζωὴν νοεράν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procl.
					<u>in Cra.</u>
					p.52
				</span></i>
			 P.</div>
